# DTF tier manifest: proxy-redirect-hold-replicas
#   (artifact-keeper#6361, 1.13.0)
# Profile-set: S3 (MinIO) with presigned redirect downloads on `backend`
# (storage.s3 + storage.s3-presigned), a second replica `backend-b` on the same
# database and bucket (topology.two-replica + topology.two-replica-s3), and
# upstreams.mock-files (a stdlib-python server on 172.16.<slot>.76 whose files
# and forced statuses the oracle sets over a control API). backend-b has no
# presign settings: it only fills the cache.
#
# THE BUG
# #6361  A presigned-redirect fast path read the proxy-cache sidecar twice: once
#        for freshness (straight from storage) and again for the Package Age
#        Policy hold (through the 30 s in-process sidecar LRU). When the second
#        read came back empty, the hold check passed and the held entry was
#        signed. The second read is empty when the entry is evicted between
#        the two reads, and, deterministically, when this replica memoised a
#        miss for the sidecar and another replica filled the entry within the
#        LRU's 30 s: the oracle drives that window. A Virtual's member
#        redirect (here a CRAN virtual over a CRAN Remote) then answered 302 to
#        a presigned URL of an object inside its hold, where the fetch paths
#        answer 409.
#
# THE GATES
#   (CONTROL) on every image: a CRAN virtual over a Remote with no hold
#             redirects a fresh cache hit (302, Location on the public S3
#             endpoint, the exact bytes): the fast path is active here;
#             the held Remote answers its cold download on backend-b 409;
#             after the LRU entry expires (31 s) backend answers the held
#             path 409.
#   (FIX)     #6361 backend memoised a sidecar miss (the upstream answered
#                   503), backend-b filled the entry inside its hold, and
#                   within the LRU's 30 s backend answers the virtual 409, not
#                   302 (RED on main: 302 to the held object).
#
# #6416  A PyPI virtual's member row whose storage_key is a proxy-cache key
#        (how releases before 1.2.0 recorded a cached file) was served with no
#        look at its cache sidecar: signed after only an existence check on
#        `backend` (presigned downloads on), streamed on `backend-b` (off, the
#        default), a HEAD included. (FIX) on both replicas a held row answers
#        409, a row whose stored scan verdict refuses it 403 (also through a
#        virtual that scans over a member that does not, #3023, and on the
#        Remote's own route), a row with no
#        sidecar or a key naming another Remote is not served (404), and a
#        stale row is not redirected to (the walk hands it to the Remote
#        path); (CONTROL) a fresh unheld row still redirects (backend)
#        and streams the exact bytes (backend-b). RED on main: 302 / 200.
# #6418  A HEAD of a fresh cached PyPI file got a redirect to a URL signed for
#        GET, which the object store refuses for a HEAD (403). (FIX) the HEAD
#        answers 200 with the file's length; (CONTROL) the GET redirects.
# #6433  Every other route that serves such a row read it with row-level
#        checks only: PyPI PEP 658 metadata through a virtual, and the package
#        routes of conda, Alpine, RPM, Debian, Go, Helm, Cargo and the generic
#        download route (a redirect on `backend`). (FIX) on each route, GET
#        and HEAD on both replicas, a held row answers 409 and a stale row is
#        not served from the row: the Remote's proxy path answers with the
#        upstream's (different) bytes, or for Helm and Cargo a non-2xx, and no
#        download is recorded against the row; the held wheel row's metadata
#        answers 409 and the
#        stale one's is not read from the row. (CONTROL) a fresh row is served
#        (backend-b, the exact bytes; the fresh wheel row's METADATA). RED on
#        main: 200 / 302.
#
# Red: main before the fix. Green: an image carrying artifact-keeper#6361
# (and #6416, #6418, #6433 for their cases).
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: admin calls back to back.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the mock upstream is on a private subnet
# (backend-b takes it from the shell; it has no CIDR allowlist).
COVERS="6361 6416 6418 6433"
PROFILES="storage.s3 storage.s3-presigned topology.two-replica topology.two-replica-s3 upstreams.mock-files"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
